			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: Person who made a big impact on your EQ life &nbsp;(Read 1586 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52" title="View the profile of Gabus">Gabus</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 268<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/psychotic-day.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I beat the Internet. The end guy was hard.<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=52"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg10437#msg10437"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg10437#msg10437">Re: Person who made a big impact on your EQ life</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #30 on:</b> August 25, 2004, 10:40:56 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							So many to think about. I would wager there are more than just the ones I can come up with off the top of my head.<br /><br />Menchu Mugabu (retired) RL friend who got me addicted to the game in the first place.<br /><br />Tolo (semi/retired) First to show me dying was hilarious, and could reap big rewards. Without him, I wouldn&#039;t have seen half of Norrath, and might even still be in Qeynos Hills.<br /><br />Herculean (semi/retired) From Herc I learned the basic skills to raiding, communication, assisting, showing up on time. How to run a casual guild successfully, and when to bow out gracefully.<br /><br />Kelce (active) One of the best guildleaders I have ever known. It is because of them that I got a chance to play a &quot;raid paladin&quot; and truly begin to fulfil my role as a paladin. I got to see content that I never thought I would. My abilites in the more refined skills, corner tanking, add tanking, prior research on strategies and tactics, and once again raid communication, I attribute to him. (whether he wants to take responsibility for that trainwreck or not)<br /><br />I am sure there are others I am forgetting, but that is the short list, and the first four that come to mind.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=139779" target="_blank">Gabus Magelo Profile</a><br />Proud member of <a href="http://Tul-Acharn.com" target="_blank">Tul Acharn</a>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg10440"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=15" title="View the profile of Killy">Killy</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Goddess of Whips and Rezzes<br />
								Moderator<br />
								Drolvarg Guardian<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/starmod.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Female.gif" alt="Female" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 427<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://home.comcast.net/~nlfalkowski/ss/clericanim02.gif" width="65" height="65" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/KillyCirce" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="KillyCirce" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://edit.yahoo.com/config/send_webmesg?.target=Lepredes"><img src="http://opi.yahoo.com/online?u=Lepredes&amp;m=g&amp;t=0" alt="Lepredes" border="0" /></a>
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=15"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.echoesineternity.org/" title="EIE" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg10440#msg10440"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg10440#msg10440">Re: Person who made a big impact on your EQ life</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #31 on:</b> August 25, 2004, 10:57:07 am &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							It has taken me a while to think but here goes my list..........<br />These people really have stood out in my eq life, and if there are names not mentioned <br />I am still thinking about you <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Smileys/Rodcet/smiley1.gif" alt="Smiley" border="0" /><br /><br />______________________________________________________________________________________________________<br />Kuxx, Qelen, for getting me started and teaching me the ways<br />Kyrro -- we have been friends since baby chars<br />Serrenity/Qenam/Moraganna and Lenlanu -- For being really nice to me and letting me tag along<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; with them back in the day just to heal and mooch xp.<br />Sorora, Slae, Pindaris, Moeh and the gang, Windor and everyone else from NSSP -- My first guild whom I loved very much and <br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; enjoyed there.<br /><br />Emalith and Vanden and Darkdoc --- When I apped to EIE, they showed me the ropes and were just very helpful and friendly.<br /><br />Dalla, Shrek, Jeet, Sazz and Phad - I give these guys (Plus Ema) lots of leadership skills.&nbsp; <br /><br />Shisouryo.........&nbsp; Come back.....!!<br /><br />Members of TA and OOD from way back that taught me my first raiding experiences......<br /><br />And last but not least..................... Sewerslop, he is very nice and calm and keeps me in check (ok maybe on 10% of the time)<br /><br />Sorry if this is alot but this who I remember making a impact on EQ to me.<br /><br /><br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" /><div align="center"><a href="http://www.magelo.com/eq_view_profile.html?num=1100304" target="_blank"><img src="http://kilaer.tripod.com/sitebuildercontent/sitebuilderpictures/kilaer-1.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a><br /><span style="color: Teal;">What we do in life, &quot;Echoes in Eternity&quot;</span></div>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
