							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg11576#msg11576"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg11576#msg11576">Re: Person who made a big impact on your EQ life</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #39 on:</b> October 04, 2004, 06:23:48 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Back pre-Kunark:&nbsp; My old perma group of Phad, Mufin, Faradorn, Dolwen, and Ashani.&nbsp; They kept me logging in when EQ life wasn&#039;t all that fun when we all turned 50 and the SolB grind wasn&#039;t too exciting anymore.&nbsp; I also have to mention my first guildleader of OoD, Solan.&nbsp; He got me feeling part of a family.<br /><br />Kunark:&nbsp; The leaders of AD.&nbsp; Corona, Eretria, Krowbar, Glayde, Keyes... so many heh.&nbsp; They tought me pretty much how to live in a raiding guild.&nbsp; They were always so full of confidence I&#039;d follow them anywhere.&nbsp; &nbsp;And Wix for the pointers when I moved from my shaman Lilli to my rogue Wuli.&nbsp; I was pretty surprised considering how he felt about twink rogues.<br /><br />PoP:&nbsp; Eelyen for giving me the experience of helping to start a new guild in Anthology (I left soon after FoT was formed).&nbsp; He had his quirks but Eel was always a strong leader that made me proud to be in Anthology when we did achieve our goals.&nbsp; Also have to mention my friends in Anth that always had a kind word when I was feeling down:&nbsp; Kaidog, Karadana, Kaiyne, Aussie, Reyem.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg11633"></a><a name="new"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=63" title="View the profile of Mordread">Mordread</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Gender: <img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/Male.gif" alt="Male" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 34<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/spawn.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								Guardian of the Crimson Flame<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=63"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:mordread_@hotmail.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg11633#msg11633"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=902.msg11633#msg11633">Re: Person who made a big impact on your EQ life</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #40 on:</b> October 07, 2004, 04:40:43 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I would have to say Corwil. He was the one who got me into Dragonflyers back in the day and thus I met the people who would shape my EQ life for a long time, good and bad.<br /><br />Kestra and Crowley who helped me with a lot of the skill building that made me into the mage I am today be it good or bad.<br /><br />Faned/Yili and Galis who helped me build on what I had started with Kestra and Crowley.<br /><br />Callador with whom I have spent a lot of EQ time.<br /><br />There are more but I think those are the ones who helped me shape my EQ life the most.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />Mordread Draconius<br />Arch Convoker of Cascade Point
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
